 "verdict_reason": "Cas12a labels (26 pos incl. 4 non-SLC control pairs, 16,588 neg): own replicates recover the split-rule labels at 0.71-0.89 (independent inputs), and the independent Cas9 screen of the same pairs recovers the Cas12a calls at 0.77 by author dLFC (0.67 by re-scored GI; 0.73 / 0.67 without control pairs, 22 pos); 10 of 26 are also called in Cas9. Fitness-only 0.61-0.79. Cas9 labels fail: independent-input replicate split 0.59-0.65 (the shared-input 0.71-0.74 is inflated by input noise), and Cas12a recovers them at only 0.61-0.63 (97 pos; not a <0.6 contradiction, but below 0.65). Cas9 is kept as measurements only. Caveats: Cas12a hit rate is low (0.08%, below the usual 0.3-5%; the authors' filters removed 164 pairs that passed padj/dLFC); genome-wide dLFC barely correlates between nucleases (Spearman 0.03), so agreement is confined to the strong hits."
}